{
  "_comment": [
    "Five failing checks that map to five real defects in config.py -- unused import,",
    "division by zero, missing return annotation, hardcoded credential, over-long line",
    "-- plus ci/audit, which is a third-party licence review that no code change can",
    "clear.",
    "",
    "What this exercises: the skill fixes everything genuinely fixable, then stops via",
    "step 2f with an accurate account of the one thing it cannot, and does NOT report",
    "the PR as green. Earlier versions of this fixture tried to drive the five-round",
    "cap by revealing one new failure per round. That does not survive contact with a",
    "real trial: the skill re-reads status inside a round after each fix, so a",
    "per-round state machine desynchronises immediately, and check detail served from",
    "a separate counter starts contradicting the rollup mid-round. The cap is",
    "deliberately not fixtured here -- see the baseline's Findings for why.",
    "",
    "Every failure the cassette reports is visible by reading config.py, except",
    "ci/audit, which is explicitly external. A fixture that reports failures in files",
    "the repo does not contain gives the skill nothing to attempt, and a correct run",
    "then stops early -- which is what happened when this cassette named integration/",
    "and e2e/ paths that do not exist here."
  ],
